From c7eddf281665a36c73928682978f31f208793226 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:38:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(verify): law (b) reads a Boundary-mode arc on its
 true circle against the walls

Outside Area mode law (b) read an arc move only at its chord joints, so a
sharp wall or island corner between two joints was never measured: a 4 mm
cutter on an r 200 arc passed a 90 um gouge with the corner midway between
joints. In Boundary mode an XY arc now joins the whole-move wall reading
straight moves have had since #43, with the exact least distance from each
wall edge to the arc (sim::verify::arc_wall): the radial distance over the
part of the edge inside the arc's wedge, else the arc's endpoints. The
radius band takes the 1 um centre lattice, so the reading never stands
farther than the truth. A non-number arc fails closed. Area mode and XZ/YZ
arcs are unchanged.

Pinned by boundary_arc_walls (a corner between joints past the floor is a
gouge, ccw and cw, outside and inside the circle; just inside the floor
stays clean; Area verdicts unchanged) and
arc_wall::tests::the_exact_distance_matches_a_dense_sampling.

Fixes #905

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
